    "result_text": "All 68 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single **`memberId`** formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (model)\n- Replaced the `customer_code` column/field with `member_id` (getter/setter `getMemberId`/`setMemberId`).\n- Deleted `getCheckDigit()` (its Luhn digit is now the CHK segment) and `getMembershipNumber()`.\n- Kept `getFiscalYear()` (`FY<YY>`) \u2014 its 2-digit year now also feeds the memberId.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced `customerCode(owner)` with `memberId(owner)` / `memberIdBase(owner)`: `REGION` (locality) + 2-digit `FY` (from `getFiscalYear()`) + `HASH8` (renamed `memberIdHash`, the same SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-upper-hex) + `CHK` (new `luhnCheckDigit` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`). Collision handling now applies to the memberId (base collision \u2192 `-<n>` suffix).\n- Set `owner.setMemberId(memberId(owner))` at create time.\n- Renamed the audit event record slot to `memberId`; `primaryIdentifier` returns the memberId; the human-readable audit line now logs `memberId` (dropping the removed fields).\n\n**Schema/spec**\n- Renamed `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` (widened to VARCHAR(32)/TEXT) across hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres schemas.\n- In `openapi.yml`, removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` and added a single readOnly `memberId` field (the generated `OwnerDto` picks this up, MapStruct maps `getMemberId` automatically).\n\nVerified: full suite `Tests run: 68, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The audit output confirms the format, e.g. `NSW277D0C08EF9` = `NSW` + `27` + `7D0C08EF` + check digit `9`.",
